**Title:** `refactor(api): migrate sync-user from JS to TypeScript with Firebase Admin token verification — replace unsafe manual JWT decode with getAuth().verifyIdToken()`

## Issue Summary

`apps/api/src/routes/auth/sync-user.handler.js` has three problems that need fixing together. First, it manually decodes the Firebase JWT payload with `Buffer.from(token.split(".")[1], "base64url")` without verifying the signature — a forged token with any chosen `uid` bypasses all auth and impersonates any user. Second, it makes multiple sequential `fetch` calls to Hasura each with manually constructed headers — repetitive, error-prone, and creates unnecessary TCP overhead. Third, it is JavaScript while the rest of `apps/api/src/` is being migrated to TypeScript (issue #311 TypeScript foundation is merged). This issue migrates the file to TypeScript, adds Firebase Admin token verification, and extracts a shared `executeGraphQL` helper that all auth handlers will use. The dev-role feature introduced in the previous issue is preserved and also typed.

